From 691c593b5612902f12024e09b90876eae7753567 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:38:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 131/252] feat(pypto-x): add W8A8-linear graph path and
 quantized weight ingestion

Contract 0002 C7 (qwen35-w8a8-graph-path):
- build_qwen35_text_decoder_graph(precision="w8a8-linear") emits graph
  contract v4: int8 weight + fp32 per-output-channel scale function
  parameters and quantize_per_token_s8 -> qmatmul_s8s8_s32 ->
  dequantize_epilogue_bf16 for the default 150 linear weights; scope=all
  covers 186; opt-in quantize_lm_head adds the section 3.4 dual packing.
- binding schema v2 / packed layout v2 now derive from the real graph:
  518 default / 554 all-linear / 520 default+lm_head / 556 full-open
  regions (ERR-0003 fixes contract section 3.1's 555 to 556).
- lowering/vector-plan/scalar+vector reference runtimes learn all four
  opcodes (multi-output quantize included); AVX2 and AVX-512 expose the
  quantize/epilogue/dequantize kernels and the int8 weight transpose as
  native packed/W8A8 planes with new fail-closed payload/ABI versions.
- AVX-512 W8A8 programs require avx512vnni; unsupported combinations stay
  fail-closed (no silent BF16 fallback, no host reference for W8A8 on
  AVX-512 without VNNI).
- coverage: w8a8_linear_coverage / whole_net_int8_compute_ratio are counted
  from the emitted operations and cross-checked against the frozen topology
  formula; the legacy static estimate stays visible for comparison.
- offline weight quantizer reproduces the C1 per-token golden bit-for-bit
  (Q1/Q2/Q3/Q5 edges included); the weighted driver gains --precision
  w8a8-linear with in-memory quantization; no weight bytes reach disk or
  evidence.
- tests: 14 new graph-path tests plus version pins updated; focused 211
  passed, full pypto_x 990 passed / 7 skipped (base 983 collected -> 997,
  only the intentional C4 -> C7 replacement test renamed).
